 "extraction": "VizieR ASU TSV export, -out=**&-out.max=unlimited. Cleaned file maps upstream columns to a standard schema (id,ra_deg,dec_deg,z,z_err,q_flag,member_flag) and appends sep_arcmin and R_proj_Mpc computed from the cluster centre with FlatLambdaCDM(H0=70,Om0=0.3). No rows dropped. Where the upstream redshift is stored as a velocity cz in km/s it is converted to z=cz/c and its uncertainty is converted consistently to dz=e_cz/c; otherwise no values are altered. Raw upstream response kept verbatim in raw/.",
 "note": "Abell 2744 (z=0.308). Richard, Claeyssens, Lagattuta et al. 2021, A&A 646, A83 ('An atlas of MUSE observations towards eight massive lensing clusters'), per-cluster table a2744. 506 spectroscopic redshifts. Quality: column zconf (redshift confidence, 1=least to 3=most secure). Column Idfrom records whether the object came from EXTERN (external prior), MUSELET (blind emission-line detection) or PRIOR (HST-continuum prior) - so the selection function is NOT magnitude-limited in a simple way: it is 'everything with a detectable feature inside the MUSE datacube'. Instrument: VLT/MUSE integral-field spectrograph. CRITICAL LIMITATION FOR sigma(R): the MUSE footprint is tiny. Coverage here reaches only ~1.9 arcmin (~0.52 Mpc projected) from the cluster centre, with 90% inside ~0.40 Mpc, and only ~138 objects fall within |dv|<3000 km/s. This catalogue therefore constrains the very inner sigma(R) only and cannot by itself produce a resolved sigma(R) profile. Combine with Owers+2011 for the outer field. Note the VizieR catalogue actually contains 12 clusters (not the 8 in the title): a2744, a370, mc257, mc329, mc416ne, mc416s, bullet, mc940, mc1206, rxj1347, smc2031, smc2131, mc2214. It does NOT contain MACS J1149, Abell S1063 or MACS J0717.",
